2F7049e982ede3aeec8bda98d3054b5a727c150341995727c32298b41a0d5e3e08.yaml?ref=a41b3dc77a15de8ceeabfcba85d60b17bad3df6b","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+fingerprints:\n+  raw_sha256: sha256:7049e982ede3aeec8bda98d3054b5a727c150341995727c32298b41a0d5e3e08\n+  normalized_sha256: sha256:7049e982ede3aeec8bda98d3054b5a727c150341995727c32298b41a0d5e3e08\n+cas_ref: sha256:7049e982ede3aeec8bda98d3054b5a727c150341995727c32298b41a0d5e3e08\n+coverage_gids: []\n+receipts:\n+  unresolved_subitems: []\n+  nonpropositional:\n+    justification: Definition 2.1 introduces the actual L2 Hilbert space, Schwartz embedding J, the operator S, its finite physical Hermite span restriction T, and the compact-test predicate Weak. These are definitions, not an assertion of graph equality, closability or existence of a physical Hilbert basis. The existing public SchwartzWeakAdjoint.Hilbert, schwartzOperator and Weak give the L2 space, actual embedded Schwartz operator and compact-test relation, using the full SchwartzCutoffGraph.differential sum. The finite restriction is the existing C := Submodule.span complex (Set.range e), T := S.domRestrict C construction in PhysicalGraphClosure.physical_graph_closure, whose physical-basis hypotheses are not discharged here. The stipulation imposes no separate square-integrability on the two differential summands. The adjacent cutoff and full-graph propositions are separate obligations.\n+    previous_atom_id: 71d57c93e85e0675c5603783058153600f6de3864a8162271185adcf305dc051\n+    next_atom_id: 92262bd336aa2b68ae8fee1dad6ed863460a70c92c92f9f932bcb6d373bd1ee2"},{"sha":"c2a86599537950791c6b6e3b49c249dd2ebd8594","filename":"Meta/Digestion/backfill/actual-oscillator-graph/nonpropositional-inapplicable/832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480.yaml","status":"added","additions":11,"deletions":0,"changes":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/a41b3dc77a15de8ceeabfcba85d60b17bad3df6b/Meta%2FDigestion%2Fbackfill%2Factual-oscillator-graph%2Fnonpropositional-inapplicable%2F832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480.yaml","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/a41b3dc77a15de8ceeabfcba85d60b17bad3df6b/Meta%2FDigestion%2Fbackfill%2Factual-oscillator-graph%2Fnonpropositional-inapplicable%2F832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480.yaml","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Meta%2FDigestion%2Fbackfill%2Factual-oscillator-graph%2Fnonpropositional-inapplicable%2F832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480.yaml?ref=a41b3dc77a15de8ceeabfcba85d60b17bad3df6b","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+fingerprints:\n+  raw_sha256: sha256:832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480\n+  normalized_sha256: sha256:832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480\n+cas_ref: sha256:832ab1c7b4d3bf3f30a0624ee840d87351226b787454144ff604812ea5e91480\n+coverage_gids: []\n+receipts:\n+  unresolved_subitems: []\n+  nonpropositional:\n+    justification: Definition 1.3 fixes positive physical parameters and defines the width, quadratic differential expression, physical Hermite formula, energies and probabilists Hermite convention; it asserts no eigenfunction, norm, orthogonality, totality or graph theorem. Reuse the public PhysicalHermiteTests.width and value with d, h := hbar, m and w := omega; SchwartzCutoffGraph.differential uses a j := h^2/(2*m j) and b j := m j*w j^2/2. The energy expression is the existing finite sum in PhysicalHermiteTests.physical_hermite_tests and PhysicalGraphClosure.physical_graph_closure. The displayed Hermite recursion and empty sum/product rules specify the polynomial and finite-index conventions, including d = 0, rather than a separate theorem. This settles the original definitions only; Hermite lowering, physical-basis properties and the explicit dimension-zero graph objective remain separate propositions.\n+ 